Subject: IR1 Implementation Substrate Boundary And Invariant Map V1
Date: 2026-05-26
Contract UUID: ee9745b5-ceed-478c-aea6-914858431d82

@ [slice_surface] docs/slices/IR1_Final_Slices.v1.sop
@ [ir1_canonical] docs/canonical/LangSOP_IR1_Final_Slices.canonical.sop
@ [implementation_readiness_surface] docs/planning/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop
@ [implementation_readiness_review] docs/reviews/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Rebake_Review.v1.sop
@ [foundation_pack] docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
@ [planning_coordination_pack] docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
@ [operations_safety_pack] docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop

& [IR1ImplementationSubstrateBoundaryAndInvariantMapV1] is the IR1-S01 boundary map for implementation substrate and repository scaffold work
  + [contract_id] is ir1-implementation-substrate-boundary-and-invariant-map-v1
  + [contract_uuid] is ee9745b5-ceed-478c-aea6-914858431d82
  + [slice_id] is IR1-S01
  + [authority_scope] is imported authority pack inventory, substrate-owned invariants, scaffold-only boundary, generated-artifact non-authority rule, downstream stale trigger list, and forbidden implementation list
  + [implementation_scope] is boundary contract only
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: define the safe edge for IR1 implementation substrate work before language, layout, test harness, or scaffold slices execute
  = must: keep all runtime behavior, parser behavior, SQLite projection behavior, LangGraph behavior, surface behavior, adapter behavior, operations simulation, operations control, and live machine control gated
  = must: preserve SOP authority files as source truth and generated artifacts as projections
  - never: create package files, install dependencies, implement runtime code, or mutate generated artifacts in this slice

& [ImportedAuthorityPackInventory: IR1] is the accepted authority inventory imported by IR1
  + [accepted_pack] is docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_pack_role] is foundation schema, operator template, storage decision, and foundation fixtures
  + [accepted_pack] is docs/planning/FSC2_Planning_Coordination_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_pack_role] is readiness, packetization, coordination, completion gate, and planning fixtures
  + [accepted_pack] is docs/planning/FSC3_Runtime_Graph_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_pack_role] is runtime graph proof contracts and trace fixture obligations
  + [accepted_pack] is docs/planning/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_pack_role] is surface projection and authority notice contracts
  + [accepted_pack] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [accepted_pack_role] is operations safety, dry-run-only, and live-control prohibition boundary
  + [accepted_readiness_surface] is docs/planning/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop
  + [accepted_readiness_review] is docs/reviews/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Rebake_Review.v1.sop

  = must: stale IR1 if any imported pack hash or readiness review hash changes without reprocessing

& [SubstrateOwnedInvariantSet] is the invariant set owned by IR1
  + [invariant] is SOP authority files remain source truth
  + [invariant] is generated SQLite, indexes, caches, build artifacts, and test outputs are projection artifacts only
  + [invariant] is code scaffold files cannot become authority records by themselves
  + [invariant] is package metadata can describe tooling but cannot authorize runtime behavior
  + [invariant] is tests can prove conformance only against accepted fixtures and explicit expected outputs
  + [invariant] is every generated artifact needs a rebuild or invalidation route
  + [invariant] is every implementation slice needs a completion review before downstream consumption
  + [invariant] is operations safety pack remains a safety boundary, not execution permission

  = must: reject downstream IR1 outputs that hide generated artifacts or promote projections to authority

& [ScaffoldOnlyImplementationBoundary] is the boundary for scaffold work that may be authorized later in IR1
  + [allowed_after_gate] is package metadata files
  + [allowed_after_gate] is project configuration files
  + [allowed_after_gate] is empty or no-op source module placeholders
  + [allowed_after_gate] is empty or no-op test module placeholders
  + [allowed_after_gate] is documentation references to accepted SOP authorities
  + [allowed_after_gate] is .gitignore entries for generated projection artifacts
  + [required_before_allowed] is IR1-S02 language runtime and tooling decision accepted
  + [required_before_allowed] is IR1-S03 repository layout and generated artifact policy accepted
  + [required_before_allowed] is IR1-S04 test harness and fixture execution shape accepted
  + [required_before_allowed] is IR1-S05 scaffold execution plan and placeholder scope accepted
  + [required_before_allowed] is IR1-S06 scaffold activation pack accepted

  = must: treat scaffold files as inert placeholders until a later implementation chunk authorizes behavior
  = must: prevent placeholder files from importing live libraries, launching processes, opening listeners, accessing secrets, or mutating resources

& [GeneratedArtifactNonAuthorityRule] is the generated artifact rule for IR1 and downstream implementation work
  + [projection_artifact] is SQLite database
  + [projection_artifact] is generated index
  + [projection_artifact] is cache file
  + [projection_artifact] is build output
  + [projection_artifact] is test output
  + [projection_artifact] is coverage output
  + [projection_artifact] is LangGraph checkpoint
  + [projection_artifact] is surface snapshot
  + [projection_artifact] is dry-run result projection
  + [required_metadata] is source_ref_set
  + [required_metadata] is generation_tool_ref
  + [required_metadata] is input_hash_set
  + [required_metadata] is generated_at
  + [required_metadata] is invalidation_rule
  + [required_metadata] is authority_limit

  = must: ignore generated artifacts as source authority unless a future SOP authority explicitly promotes a record through accepted processing
  = must: delete or rebuild generated artifacts when their input hash set changes

& [DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR1] is the stale trigger list for IR1 downstream slices
  + [stale_trigger] is change to post-FSC5 implementation readiness canonical specification
  + [stale_trigger] is change to post-FSC5 implementation readiness surface
  + [stale_trigger] is change to post-FSC5 rebake review
  + [stale_trigger] is change to IR1 final slice surface
  + [stale_trigger] is change to IR1-S01 boundary map
  + [stale_trigger] is change to accepted language runtime and tooling decision
  + [stale_trigger] is change to accepted repository layout and generated artifact policy
  + [stale_trigger] is change to accepted test harness and fixture execution shape
  + [stale_trigger] is change to accepted scaffold execution plan
  + [stale_trigger] is any generated artifact treated as authority
  + [stale_trigger] is any package, test, or placeholder file performing runtime behavior before authorization
  + [stale_trigger] is any operations control or live machine control leak

  = must: rerun completion review before downstream slices consume stale substrate assumptions

& [ForbiddenImplementationList: IR1-S01] is the forbidden implementation list for this slice
  + [forbidden_scope] is language/package installation
  + [forbidden_scope] is code scaffolding
  + [forbidden_scope] is parser implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is SQLite builder implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is generated index creation
  + [forbidden_scope] is executable test harness implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is LangGraph runtime implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is UI or surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is operations simulator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope] is command execution beyond repository inspection and verification commands
  + [forbidden_scope] is process control
  + [forbidden_scope] is GPU control
  + [forbidden_scope] is model runtime mutation
  + [forbidden_scope] is job dispatch
  + [forbidden_scope] is credential access or mutation
  + [forbidden_scope] is network exposure mutation
  + [forbidden_scope] is destructive filesystem action
  + [forbidden_scope] is persistent operations automation
  + [forbidden_scope] is live machine control

  = must: reject IR1-S01 if any forbidden implementation scope appears in the output

& [IR1S01CoverageReview] is the coverage checklist for IR1-S01
  + [imported_authority_pack_inventory_present] is ImportedAuthorityPackInventory: IR1
  + [substrate_owned_invariant_set_present] is SubstrateOwnedInvariantSet
  + [scaffold_only_boundary_present] is ScaffoldOnlyImplementationBoundary
  + [generated_artifact_non_authority_rule_present] is GeneratedArtifactNonAuthorityRule
  + [downstream_stale_trigger_list_present] is DownstreamStaleTriggerList: IR1
  + [forbidden_implementation_list_present] is ForbiddenImplementationList: IR1-S01
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is package installation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is runtime code
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is parser implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is SQLite builder implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is LangGraph implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is surface implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is adapter implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations simulator implementation
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is operations control
  + [forbidden_scope_absent] is live machine control

  = must: open IR1-S02 only after this boundary map is accepted by completion review
